 "description": "Tier-1 default-resolution cases: each is a ServerArgs a target scenario hands SGLang, run through SGLang's own resolution on CPU with the chip's CUDA platform restored (oracle/run_serverargs.py). Chip facts are the device's own reports, each with its source; models are configuration only, at a pinned revision. Chips named probe-*GiB are boundary probes: a memory exactly at a threshold of memory_hook.py, not a device; they let a case tell a < from a <=. Cases past the first 25 were added so that every branch an accepted input can reach changes an answer (the mutation sweep, oracle/mutate.py).",
